Servlet --> providing connectivity to frontend
front react UI

App --> service --> DAO --> database

servlet  --->

react UI(GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) ---> servlet --> service(processed) ---> DAO---> database

GET --> read data
POST --> create data/ adding new data
PUT --> update data
DELETE --> delete data

REST API ----> Representational State Transfer
rule
1. HTTP methods define the operation --> get, post, put, del
2. URL identifies the resourse
    /api/user
    /api/product
    /apt/user/{id}
    /api/product/121

    user serlet class ---> /api/user/*
        adduser --> /api/user/id....
        update ---> /api/user/1
        delete --> /api/user/121
    product servlet class ---> /api/product/*
         adduser --> /api/product/id....
        update ---> /api/product/1
            delete --> /api/product/121

3. Data is exchanged in the form of json
{
    ""
}

4. HTTP status code --> tell the result
200 --> success
201 --> created suucesfully
400 --> Bad request
404 --> data not found
500 --> server error



//servlet
---doGet(), doPOST(), doPut(), doDelete() --Httpservlet class --> GenericServlet class




